id: pm-hdvxqg
title: "GH-1519: preflight test run options before persisting linked-test edits"
description: "https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/issues/1519 reports on published 2026.10.20/plain non-Git trackers that test --add persists a link before refusing invalid --timeout, --pm-context, --env-set or --only-index values, so retries accumulate duplicate registrations. It also reports run counters on add-only --progress and generic errors for some invalid values. This is reporter evidence; current-head reproduction and implementation remain pending. The scope is admission of the entire requested link/run option combination before any write, beyond the earlier linked-context validation."
type: Issue
status: in_progress
priority: 1
tags[3]: agent-ux,"area:testing",mutation-safety
created_at: "2026-10-20T10:34:31.518Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-20T12:36:16.656Z"
assignee: "harness:codex"
claim_principal: "harness:codex#195da4edbf99e3a7d3dcd1aa"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 180
acceptance_criteria: "Exercise invalid timeout, context, environment and index options through CLI and native SDK with add/remove edits: preflight refusals must leave item bytes, links and history unchanged and name the offending flag/value with an honest no-change receipt. Define run-only options on registration-only calls consistently, including progress output without fabricated execution counters. Preserve valid add-plus-run behavior, audit real executed failures truthfully, and keep existing context-intake/refusal semantics intact; do not equate a real post-admission child failure with a preflight refusal."
goal: Make linked-test registration and execution safe for autonomous retries.
objective: Validate the complete request and effective selection before saving linked-test edits.
value: A usage refusal cannot leave hidden links or history that retries would duplicate.
why_now: GH-1519 reproduces persistent side effects after invalid options on the current public package.
parent: pm-33cw
risk: medium
confidence: medium
expected_result: "Agents can safely retry invalid test-link requests without hidden edits or duplicates, while accepted registrations and genuine executions retain truthful mutation/run receipts."
